  "prefLabel": "En 1004.02 Completeness Review",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1004.02 Completeness Review. The utility shall record the date and time of the application’s receipt. The utility shall notify the applicant within 3 business days that the application has been received. Within 10 business days of receipt, the utility shall notify the applicant whether the application is complete. If the application is incomplete, the utility shall provide the applicant with a list of all information that the applicant needs to provide to complete the initial application. The applicant shall provide the requested information within 10 business days for the simplified and fast track processes and 20 business days for the standard process, or the application shall be deemed withdrawn.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
